# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

## [0.4.0] - 2026-03-20
### Changed
- **Project Rebranding:** VetCore → MarketCoreSoft
  - Renamed Django project module from `vetcore` to `marketcore`
  - Updated all branding, templates, and documentation
- **Removed Clinical Module:**
  - Deleted `clinical` app entirely (models, views, urls, templates, signals, forms, admin)
  - Removed `Patient` model and all related views, forms, serializers, URLs, templates
  - Removed veterinary-specific features: medical records, consultations, attachments, appointments/schedule
  - Removed `clinical_required` decorator
- **Removed Vetter Import:**
  - Deleted `vetter_import.py` service and related views/templates
  - Removed import hub and Vetter-specific URLs
- **Adapted User Roles:**
  - Changed roles from `VET`/`ADMIN` to `CASHIER`/`ADMIN`
  - Removed `license_number` field from `UserProfile`
  - Updated all forms and templates to reflect new role structure
- **Cloud API:**
  - Changed tenant types from `VET`/`SUPPLIER`/`BOTH` to `RETAIL`/`WHOLESALE`/`BOTH`
  - Rebranded API name and logging
- **Updated Configuration:**
  - Docker containers renamed (`marketcore_desktop`, `marketcore_saas`, `marketcore_db_saas`)
  - Environment variables renamed (`VETCORE_MODE` → `MARKETCORE_MODE`)
  - License URLs updated for new domain
  - Removed Vetter volume mount from Docker Compose
- **Documentation:**
  - Rewrote README.MD for retail/business focus
  - Rewrote ROADMAP.md with retail-oriented phases
  - Updated CHANGELOG

## [0.3.0] - 2026-03-18
### Added
- **Cloud API — Modular Architecture:**
  - Refactored from monolithic 3-endpoint app to modular structure (core/, models/, routers/)
  - JWT admin authentication (`POST /admin/login` → token)
  - License management endpoints: check, create/renew, revoke, list (JWT-protected)
  - Health check with database connectivity status (`GET /health`)
  - Rate limiting with slowapi
  - CORS configuration
  - Request logging middleware
  - Backward-compatible `/check-license` endpoint for existing Desktop clients
  - Swagger/OpenAPI docs at `/docs`
- **Database Migrations:**
  - Alembic setup with autogenerate support
  - Initial migration: licenses, releases, tenants tables
- **Models:**
  - `License`: hardware_id, client_name, expiration_date, is_active, timestamps
  - `Release`: version, download_url, changelog, is_active
  - `Tenant`: name, type, tax_id, contact info, plan, region
- **Docker:**
  - cloud_api volume mount for hot-reload development
  - JWT_SECRET, DEBUG, CORS_ORIGINS, RATE_LIMIT_DEFAULT env vars
- **Config:**
  - Centralized settings via pydantic-settings (`core/config.py`)

## [0.2.0] - 2026-03-17
### Added
- **Point of Sale (POS):**
  - Cart-based sales workflow
  - Barcode scanner support (camera via html5-qrcode + USB reader)
  - Payment method tracking, sale detail view with print option
- **Cash Register Reports:**
  - Daily/shift-based cash closing with payment method breakdown
- **Team Management:**
  - Multi-user with roles, employee CRUD, activate/deactivate, password reset
  - PIN-based quick user switching, lockscreen, user avatars
- **Settings Hub:**
  - Company configuration (name, tax ID, currency, language)
  - Backup/restore SQLite databases
- **Internationalization (i18n):**
  - Spanish, English, Portuguese with per-company language setting
- **Search & Pagination:**
  - Server-side search on client list, paginated results
- **Inventory Enhancements:**
  - QR label printing for products, barcode field on Product model
- **License System:**
  - Offline + online license validation with 3-day grace period

### Changed
- **Architecture:** Hybrid Desktop (SQLite) + SaaS (PostgreSQL) architecture
- **Docker Compose:** 5-service setup

## [0.1.0] - 2026-01-30
### Added
- **Infrastructure:** Docker + Docker Compose setup (Django + PostgreSQL)
- **Core:** Client management with CRUD
- **Inventory:** Products & Services module with stock movement tracking
- **Frontend:** Django Templates with Bootstrap 5
- **Dashboard:** Home panel with quick access shortcuts
- **API:** Basic REST endpoints with Django Rest Framework (DRF)
